From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Realer Mason <stone-mason@dr.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:02:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] drm/rockchip: apply the RK3588 prescan sync width
 minimum

The RK3588 vendor driver clamps the prescan horizontal sync interval to
eight pixels. The shared RK3568 setup currently writes the mode's sync
width directly, so a six-pixel sync on the ATK 1080p panel programs a
prescan interval below the vendor minimum.

Apply the clamp for RK3588 without changing the transmitted mode timing
or the behaviour of other VOP2 variants. Verified the VP3 prescan register
changes from 0x024f0006 to the vendor value 0x024f0008 on this board while
GPU rendering and VOP writeback continue to produce the interface image.

Signed-off-by: Realer Mason <stone-mason@dr.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
index 17eda592b1833aff84927d93a093b4d26c5cfb18..a7215ff8939a5ed9ee806167e23a7b2605b25696 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
@@ -2457,6 +2457,10 @@ static void rk3568_vop2_setup_bg_dly(struct vop2_video_port *vp)
 	u32 bg_dly;
 	u32 pre_scan_dly;
 
+	/* RK3588 needs at least eight pixels in the prescan sync interval. */
+	if (vp->vop2->version == VOP_VERSION_RK3588)
+		hsync_len = max_t(u16, hsync_len, 8);
+
 	bg_dly = vp->data->pre_scan_max_dly[3];
 	vop2_writel(vp->vop2, RK3568_VP_BG_MIX_CTRL(vp->id),
 		    FIELD_PREP(RK3568_VP_BG_MIX_CTRL__BG_DLY, bg_dly));
